# Human-owned knobs for the five reference books.
#
# RUNG LADDER — raise ONE rung at a time, each a deliberate human edit:
#   RUNG-0  DRY_RUN=1  EXECUTION=simulator   compute + log targets only
#   RUNG-1  DRY_RUN=0  EXECUTION=simulator   live shadow ledger, no orders sent
#   RUNG-2  DRY_RUN=0  EXECUTION=ibkr        real orders to the IBKR PAPER account
#
# CURRENT RUNG: RUNG-2, armed 2026-08-31 on explicit instruction.
#
# WHAT THESE ARE. B1/B3/B4/B5/B6 are reference books, NOT alpha claims. They
# exist so a strategy sleeve is measured against what you earn with zero skill
# through the identical order, fill and accounting path. They were funded
# 2026-07-30 and then never ran: no launchd job was ever created for them, so
# for 22 business days the comparison series this project measures itself
# against was a flat line at its funding value. That is what arming fixes.
#
# B2, B7 and B8 need SHORT legs, which static_weights forbids, so they remain
# shadow books in results/bench/ rather than live orders.
#
# SHARED TICKER — READ BEFORE CHANGING THE SPECS. bench_b1_hyg and
# bench_b6_ew_credit BOTH hold HYG, so fill attribution by symbol is ambiguous
# for that one ticker. It is resolved by the orderId -> sleeve map the adapter
# writes at placement (_ibkr_shadow/_order_map.csv). If that map is missing, a
# shared-ticker fill is reported UNATTRIBUTED and dropped, never guessed.
# Add another ticker overlap and you inherit the same requirement.
#
# NOT IDEMPOTENT: each armed run stacks another order set at the broker, there
# is no dedupe. Cancel pending orders before re-running by hand.
#
# Client id 46 (cef=45, phase0=17). capture_fills uses id+50, so 96 here.
# Scheduled 17:25, ten minutes behind cef, so two books never contend for TWS.

DRY_RUN=0
EXECUTION=ibkr
BOOK=/Users/simonjarvis/Desktop/2027/QUANTT/2027/ops/books/benchmarks_book.json
BOOKS_ROOT=/Users/simonjarvis/Desktop/2027/QUANTT/2027/ops/books/benchmarks_live
